      "end": 620,
      "start": 0,
      "text": "Zomba, Malawi\nZomba is a city in southern Malawi , in the Shire Highlands . It is the administrative capital of Zomba District . It was the capital of first British Central Africa and then Nyasaland before the establishment of the Republic of Malawi in 1964 . It was also the first capital of Malawi and remained so until 1974 , when Lilongwe became the capital . The Parliament remained even longer , until 1994 in Zomba . The city is best known for its British colonial architecture and its location at the base of the dramatic Zomba Plateau . Zomba is also the home of Chancellor College of the University of Malawi ."
     }
